# TSEK environment variables: where each one lives.
# No real values belong in this repository, in any file or any commit.
#
# Local development: copy the per-app examples and fill them in:
#   backend/.env.example  -> backend/.env         (server secrets, never committed)
#   frontend/.env.example -> frontend/.env.local  (public build settings only)
#
# Staging and production: set values in each host's dashboard, scoped to that
# environment, with separate keys per environment:
#   Render (backend):   DATABASE_URL, DIRECT_DATABASE_URL, OPENAI_API_KEY,
#                       OPENAI_MODEL, JWT_SECRET, FRONTEND_URL, PORT
#   Vercel (frontend):  VITE_SERVICES_ENDPOINT (optional)
#   Neon (database):    one branch per environment (main = production, staging)
#   OpenAI:             separate staging key with a monthly spending limit
#
# GitHub Actions: Settings -> Environments -> staging / production
#   Secrets:   VERCEL_DEPLOY_HOOK_URL, RENDER_DEPLOY_HOOK_URL
#   Variables: FRONTEND_URL, BACKEND_HEALTHCHECK_URL, DATABASE_CHECK_URL
# Repository secret: AI_REVIEW_OPENAI_API_KEY (pull request AI review only)
#
# If a key leaks: rotate it first in the provider dashboard, then tell the team.
